{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310765,"nonce":"w5FiOPhP1zJpj0CFM2vZKNmVUqo=","title":"Send/Sync derive system — explicit @:derive is now a CHECKED claim (field soundness in analysis phase); String is Send+Sync+Clone","message":"`@:derive([Send])`/`([Sync])` trait system — three shipped pieces (branch feat/llama-prefill-graph):\n\n- **Cross-file persistence (e13c6304):** derives mirrored onto the class/interface **symbol** at lowering (`SymbolFlags::DERIVE_SEND=1\u003c\u003c23 / DERIVE_SYNC=1\u003c\u003c24`, accessors `derives_send()/derives_sync()`). `SendSyncValidator` only sees this file's `typed_file.classes`, so a `@:derive` extern used at a Thread.spawn site in another module resolves via the shared symbol table, not the local class list.\n- **Interfaces (0cb07a4d):** `@:derive` works on interfaces too; `TypeKind::Interface{symbol_id}` shares the class trait path (`class_implements_trait` → `find_class` misses → falls through to symbol flags). An interface-typed value is Send at a capture site.\n- **Field soundness (ecef81d9):** `SendSyncValidator::validate_derive_soundness` — a class that explicitly derives Send/Sync must have every field fulfill the trait, else E0302 (`X derives Send but field f (type Dynamic) is not Send`). Runs in the **analysis phase (post-lowering)** so forward-ref field types + cross-file flags are resolved — NOT during lowering. Wired into BOTH `compilation.rs` (~5421, the path `rayzor run` executes — the OTHER pipeline type_checking_pipeline.rs:311 is not on that path) AND type_checking_pipeline. **Extern classes are SKIPPED** — opaque fields, derive = vouched-for promise (e.g. sys.net.SocketOutput wraps an OS fd).\n\n**Model shape:** explicit `@:derive` = CHECKED claim at declaration (field soundness) + trusted at use sites (`class_implements_trait` returns true on explicit derive without re-checking fields). Auto-derive (no annotation) is the field-recursion path (`auto_derive_send/sync`). Both agree once the declaration is validated sound.\n\n**String is Send + Sync + Clone (NOT Copy)** — trait_checker.rs `implements_trait`. `HaxeString` = plain ptr+len+cap, no cached/interior-mutable state (`haxe_string_hash` recomputes FNV-1a each call, caches nothing), so a shared `\u0026String` is race-free, matching Rust's `String`. The old \"not Sync (interior mutability)\" note was stale; under the checked model it would have forbidden every `Arc`-shared struct with a String field. **TRIPWIRE:** if String ever gains interior mutability (COW buffer, cached hash field), revisit is_sync(String) and re-gate. Unit test = `test_string_is_send_sync_clone_not_copy`.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_shared_needs_arc_clone_on_bind]], [[project_shared_arc_tensors]], [[feature_extern_method_bodies_and_env_split]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `feature_derive_send_sync_field_soundness` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}